    "publishedAt": "2026-11-16",
    "summary": "Collaboration Brings Together Complimentary CXL-based and Photonic Memory Technologies to Unlock Greater Memory Capacity SANTA CLARA, Calif. (NASDAQ: MRVL), a leader in data infrastructure semiconductor solutions and Penguin Solutions, Inc . Together, these approaches are designed to provide customers with greater flexibility to expand memory capacity and scale AI infrastructure as its needs evolve, offering a single upgrade path from direct-attach expansion to disaggregated, multi-rack sharing, without re-architecting their infrastructure at each step. By combining CXL-based memory expansion with a roadmap to optical memory sharing, Marvell and Penguin Solutions are giving CIOs and AI data center leaders a practical path to improve accelerator utilization which directly leads to increased token revenue, eases pressure from constrained HBM and DDR5 supply and builds more flexible AI memory architectures without wholesale infrastructure replacement.",
